== demo: golden master of legacy_monthly_contribution(), the TS rewrite checked against it ==

## 1. Generate inputs
   concept: boundary values on every threshold the code might have (cap, offset, minimum, birthdays, join days, leap years) plus seeded random cases
   352 boundary + 1000 random (seed 2026) = 1352 cases

## 2. Record the golden master
   concept: run every input through the legacy PL/pgSQL and keep the outputs in a committed approval file; the legacy output is the spec
   legacy outputs differing from approved/legacy.approved.tsv: 0
   1352 approved cases, 276 of them 0.00

## 3. The rewrite from the booklet, against the golden master
   concept: the written rules (5/7/9% of salary above 6,000 capped at 150,000, rounded, from the month of joining) are not what the system does
   676 of 1352 cases differ
