   #86    salary   48000.00  born 1980-06-15  joined 2024-02-16  period 2024-02-01  legacy     0.00  rewrite   245.00
   #966   salary   17983.98  born 1976-03-07  joined 2024-05-23  period 2026-03-01  legacy    89.87  rewrite    69.91

## 4. Discover the rules from the mismatches
   concept: turn each pattern into a hypothesis, switch it on in the rewrite, and keep it if it reproduces legacy; a mismatch is explained by the smallest set that does
    417  truncateToCent
    114  capSalaryBeforeOffset
     53  midMonthCutoff
     41  ageByDaysOver365
     38  deMinimis
     12  truncateToCent + deMinimis
      1  ageByDaysOver365 + truncateToCent

## 5. Decide per rule: keep the quirk or fix it on purpose
   concept: kept rules become the rewrite's behaviour; fixed ones go on an allowlist with a reason, so their mismatches are expected and nothing else is
   KEEP midMonthCutoff        payroll closes on the 15th; the booklet never said so, but every employer's payroll relies on it
   KEEP capSalaryBeforeOffset the cap is on the payroll salary field; the booklet's wording was ambiguous and 15 years of statements follow legacy
   FIX  ageByDaysOver365      legacy counts age as days / 365, so leap days make members older: up to 9 days before a 35th birthday and 13 before a 50th they pay the higher rate
   KEEP truncateToCent        employers deduct the truncated amount; rounding would open a 0.01 reconciliation difference on about half the members every month
   KEEP deMinimis             collecting it costs more than it is worth; it is in the employer agreement, not in the booklet

## 6. The final rewrite, against the golden master
   concept: equal, or differing only where a documented fix says it must; zero unexplained mismatches is the green bar
   1352 cases: 1310 equal, 42 allowlisted (ageByDaysOver365), 0 unexplained
   #63    salary   48000.00  born 1989-02-02  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy   245.00  rewrite   175.00
   #64    salary   48000.00  born 1989-02-03  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy   245.00  rewrite   175.00
   #65    salary   48000.00  born 1989-02-09  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy   245.00  rewrite   175.00
   #73    salary   48000.00  born 1974-02-02  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy   315.00  rewrite   245.00

## 7. The golden master catches a regression
   concept: someone 'tidies' the truncation into rounding: those mismatches are on no allowlist, so the check goes red
   430 unexplained mismatches, for example:
   #21    salary    7333.33  born 1965-06-15  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy     0.00  rewrite    10.00
   #26    salary    7714.28  born 1980-06-15  joined 2010-01-04  period 2024-02-01  legacy     0.00  rewrite    10.00

## 8. The decision table
   concept: what was learned, written for people: one row per rule, with where it came from and what was decided
   | # | When | Then | Source | Decision |
   | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   | R1 | salary is 0 or less | 0.00 | booklet | |
   | R2 | joined after the last day of the period | 0.00 | booklet | |
   | R3 | joined in the period's month after the 15th | 0.00 for that month | legacy, 53 mismatches | keep: payroll closes on the 15th; the booklet never said so, but every employer's payroll relies on it |
   | R4 | salary above 150,000.00 | pensionable = min(salary, 150,000.00) - 6,000.00, so at most 144,000.00 | legacy, 114 mismatches | keep: the cap is on the payroll salary field; the booklet's wording was ambiguous and 15 years of statements follow legacy |
   | R5 | age on the 1st of the period: under 35 / 35 to 49 / 50 and over | rate 5% / 7% / 9% of pensionable salary | legacy, 42 mismatches | fix: legacy counts age as days / 365, so leap days make members older: up to 9 days before a 35th birthday and 13 before a 50th they pay the higher rate |
   | R6 | pensionable x rate / 12 has more than 2 decimals | truncated to the cent, never rounded up | legacy, 430 mismatches | keep: employers deduct the truncated amount; rounding would open a 0.01 reconciliation difference on about half the members every month |
   | R7 | the monthly amount is under 10.00 | 0.00 | legacy, 50 mismatches | keep: collecting it costs more than it is worth; it is in the employer agreement, not in the booklet |

